#### Interpretation

The wedge is real even before manual audit: token edits 0/20 versus free-form rewrites 5/20 (judge-raw) means the probe direction *can* be exploited from input space — but only with enough freedom to rewrite, not just nudge tokens. The probe captures something real that an attacker can reach, just not via the single-token attribution surface.

This complicates the Level-2A negative result. The probe is *not* purely correlational — there's a causal handle accessible from input space. It just isn't the handle the attribution map points at. The remaining question (deferred to manual review) is how many of the 5 judge-flagged flips survive the same audit standard we applied in 2C, since intent-preserving paraphrases are far less likely to produce ablation-style gibberish but can still produce structurally-fluent deflection.

